  "summary": "All five patients are reconciled under RBC-TOC-02, with a signed progress note for each. New results and documents came in while I worked, and four of my earlier decisions changed because of them. Each change is recorded in a follow-up note.\n\nWalter Kim\n- Furosemide changed to 40 mg twice daily, per the signed addendum. An unsigned draft addendum saying 60 mg twice daily arrived later; I ignored it because it isn't part of the signed record.\n- Potassium chloride stopped, per the discharge summary.\n- Omeprazole kept. Pantoprazole was only a hospital formulary substitute, so I didn't order it.\n- Lisinopril: I first kept it on hold because his 10/21 potassium was 5.4. His repeat panel on 10/23 showed potassium 4.7 and creatinine 1.21, which meets the discharge condition, so I resumed it.\n- The task I made you to review his potassium (task-t0003) is no longer needed. The system wouldn't let me cancel it, so please close it.\n- Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin unchanged.\n\nTerence Stark\n- Carvedilol: the summary said 12.5 mg twice daily and I ordered that. A signed addendum then reversed it because of a slow heart rate (48–52) and lightheadedness on standing. He's back on 6.25 mg twice daily.\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 unchanged.\n- **Flag – atorvastatin:** his fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission. I left the order unchanged and messaged you.\n- **Flag – glipizide:** he's been filling glipizide 5 mg from an outside endocrinologist (Dr. Desai), and the discharge summary doesn't mention it. I ordered nothing and messaged you.\n\nEarnest Roberts\n- Lisinopril: I resumed it because creatinine was 1.08 and potassium 4.6 on 10/22. A potassium of 5.5 then came in from 10/23, so I put it back on hold.\n- **Flag:** please review his next potassium before restarting lisinopril; there's a task for you due 10/26.\n- Insulin glargine, insulin lispro and rosuvastatin unchanged.\n\nGerald Whitcomb\n- Lisinopril: I resumed it because creatinine was 1.12 and potassium 4.4 on 10/21. A potassium of 5.4 drawn 10/22 then arrived, so I put it back on hold.\n- **Flag:** please review his next potassium before restarting lisinopril; there's a task for you due 10/26.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nLorraine Pruitt\n- Metformin stays on hold. Its only creatinine (1.21) was drawn in hospital, and the restart condition requires a post-discharge result.\n- **Flag:** her post-discharge panel is due 10/24; there's a task for you that day to review it and decide on restarting metformin.\n- Amlodipine and atorvastatin unchanged.\n\nI closed the five new-result and document items in your inbox, linking each to what I did. Nothing else came in for these patients.",
